{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"9dcce8cf-c317-480d-8347-97a47847af80","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/runtime-read-capability-split/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"tests/unit/core/step/capability-consumers.test.ts","title":"TC-005 / TC-020 (must): detectNoOp + listChangedFiles unavailable path not directly tested","rationale":"test-cases.md TC-005 and TC-020 (both priority: must) require a test that passes { kind: 'unavailable' } to detectNoOp and verifies the resulting behavior. The capability-consumers.test.ts TC-004 only tests { kind: 'success', files: [] }. The code path (result.kind !== 'success' → changedFiles = []) is documented in a comment but not directly exercised by any unit test. Additionally, the TC-005 title ('no-op とみなさない') contradicts the scenario name ('変更ファイルは空として扱われる') and the actual code behavior (unavailable → empty changedFiles → no-op detected), suggesting a title error that should be fixed alongside the test addition.","line":51},{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"tests/unit/core/step/capability-consumers.test.ts","title":"TC-010 / TC-021 (must): derivePriorRoundContext null-degrade paths not directly tested at iteration≥2","rationale":"TC-010 ('listCommitChangedFiles が absent のとき null を返す') and TC-021 ('listCommitChangedFiles が unavailable のとき prior-round-context が null を返す') are priority: must. The existing TC-009 test uses iteration=1 which triggers the early guard (iteration < 2 → null) before reaching the listCommitChangedFiles check. No test exercises the path where iteration≥2 and a priorOid is resolvable but listCommitChangedFiles is absent or returns unavailable. The code handles both paths correctly (lines 143–147 of prior-round-context.ts) but the must-priority TC coverage is missing.","line":118},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/archive/__tests__/achieved-assurance.test.ts","title":"Stale comment references Pick<RuntimeStrategy, 'readFileAtCommit'> after T-08 changed it to an explicit interface","rationale":"Line 140 reads '// The AssuranceProvenanceRuntime is narrowed to Pick<RuntimeStrategy, \"readFileAtCommit\">.' but T-08 (design D3) changed AssuranceProvenanceRuntime from a Pick type alias to an explicit consumer-owned interface in achieved-assurance.ts. The comment is factually incorrect and may mislead future readers.","line":140}],"evidence":{"checked":14,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/step/spec-review.ts","title":"prepareRoundContext still typed as RuntimeStrategy | undefined — acceptable per D7","rationale":"spec-review.ts imports RuntimeStrategy and declares prepareRoundContext(... runtimeStrategy: RuntimeStrategy | undefined). It passes this value directly to derivePriorRoundContext which now accepts CommitInspectionCapability | undefined. This works via structural typing (RuntimeStrategy satisfies CommitInspectionCapability). spec-review is an orchestration step not in the target list, and D7 explicitly preserves RuntimeStrategy | undefined for orchestration layers. No action needed.","line":104},{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/step/scope-check.ts","title":"deps.runtimeStrategy typed as optional property (?) vs design doc's union (| undefined)","rationale":"Design D5 specifies 'runtimeStrategy: ChangedFilesCapability | undefined' but the implementation uses 'runtimeStrategy?: ChangedFilesCapability' (optional property). In TypeScript these have subtly different assignability semantics but the runtime behavior and structural compatibility with PipelineDeps are identical. The functional guard 'if (!deps.runtimeStrategy)' handles both absent and undefined cases correctly. No behavioral issue.","line":43}]},"followUpAttempts":1,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":1}},"startedAt":"2026-08-30T05:33:09.590Z","endedAt":"2026-08-30T05:40:02.431Z","commitOid":"030d052fff7c1cc2bf6e215811c0249e89c33a00"}
